For the cofactor $f_{x_{1}}=x_{3}+x_{4}$ we can use the BDD from Figure 8.20b . But for the cofactor $f_{\bar{x}_{1}}=x_{2} x_{4}+x_{2} x_{3}+\bar{x}_{2} x_{3} x_{4}$ it is useful to apply Shannon's expansion again, with respect to input $x_{2}$ . This gives

$$
f _ {\bar {x} _ {1} \bar {x} _ {2}} = 0 \cdot x _ {4} + 0 \cdot x _ {3} + 1 \cdot x _ {3} x _ {4} = x _ {3} x _ {4}
$$

